// XFAIL: RT-370: a `const fn` whose body calls a non-const fn (`println`, a program's `fn g`) is accepted; rustc refuses both (E0015, cannot call non-const function in constant functions) (0.30.2)
// rustc E0015 at lines 17 and 22 (twin .rs.txt). vole checks and builds
// it and prints `f runs` and `2 3`; v0.28.0 to v0.30.1 the same. RT-119
// and RT-180 are a const's and a static's value calling a non-const fn;
// RT-194 a const fn call in a const that is never evaluated at compile
// time; here the const fn's own body is never held to constness, so a
// `const A: u8 = f(4);` runs f's println at each use of A (scratch
// ce/d2.vl: `f runs` twice).
// ERROR: line 17
// ERROR: line 22
// ERROR-COUNT: 2
fn g(x: u8) -> u8 {
    x + 1
}

const fn f(x: u8) -> u8 {
    println("f runs");
    x + 1
}

const fn k(x: u8) -> u8 {
    g(x)
}

fn main() {
    println("{} {}", f(1), k(2));
}
